   1:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_wwdg.c **** /**
   2:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_wwdg.c ****   ******************************************************************************
   3:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_wwdg.c ****   * @file    stm32f4xx_wwdg.c
   4:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_wwdg.c ****   * @author  MCD Application Team
   5:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_wwdg.c ****   * @version V1.8.0
   6:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_wwdg.c ****   * @date    04-November-2016
   7:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_wwdg.c ****   * @brief   This file provides firmware functions to manage the following 
   8:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_wwdg.c ****   *          functionalities of the Window watchdog (WWDG) peripheral:           
   9:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_wwdg.c ****   *           + Prescaler, Refresh window and Counter configuration
  10:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_wwdg.c ****   *           + WWDG activation
  11:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_wwdg.c ****   *           + Interrupts and flags management
  12:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_wwdg.c ****   *             
  13:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_wwdg.c ****  @verbatim    
  14:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_wwdg.c ****  ===============================================================================
  15:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_wwdg.c ****                            ##### WWDG features #####
  16:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_wwdg.c ****  ===============================================================================
  17:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_wwdg.c ****     [..]                                      
  18:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_wwdg.c ****         Once enabled the WWDG generates a system reset on expiry of a programmed
  19:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_wwdg.c ****         time period, unless the program refreshes the counter (downcounter) 
  20:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_wwdg.c ****         before to reach 0x3F value (i.e. a reset is generated when the counter
  21:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_wwdg.c ****         value rolls over from 0x40 to 0x3F). 
  22:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_wwdg.c ****         An MCU reset is also generated if the counter value is refreshed
  23:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_wwdg.c ****         before the counter has reached the refresh window value. This 
  24:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_wwdg.c ****         implies that the counter must be refreshed in a limited window.
  25:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_wwdg.c ****               
  26:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_wwdg.c ****         Once enabled the WWDG cannot be disabled except by a system reset.
  27:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_wwdg.c ****           
  28:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_wwdg.c ****         WWDGRST flag in RCC_CSR register can be used to inform when a WWDG
  29:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_wwdg.c ****         reset occurs.
  30:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_wwdg.c ****              
ARM GAS  /tmp/ccrFLH1I.s 			page 2


  31:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_wwdg.c ****         The WWDG counter input clock is derived from the APB clock divided 
  32:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_wwdg.c ****         by a programmable prescaler.
  33:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_wwdg.c ****                 
  34:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_wwdg.c ****         WWDG counter clock = PCLK1 / Prescaler
  35:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_wwdg.c ****         WWDG timeout = (WWDG counter clock) * (counter value)
  36:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_wwdg.c ****                        
  37:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_wwdg.c ****         Min-max timeout value @42 MHz(PCLK1): ~97.5 us / ~49.9 ms
  38:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_wwdg.c ****                              
  39:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_wwdg.c ****                       ##### How to use this driver #####
  40:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_wwdg.c ****  ===============================================================================
  41:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_wwdg.c ****     [..]
  42:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_wwdg.c ****       (#) Enable WWDG clock using RCC_APB1PeriphClockCmd(RCC_APB1Periph_WWDG, ENABLE) function
  43:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_wwdg.c ****               
  44:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_wwdg.c ****       (#) Configure the WWDG prescaler using WWDG_SetPrescaler() function
  45:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_wwdg.c ****                              
  46:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_wwdg.c ****       (#) Configure the WWDG refresh window using WWDG_SetWindowValue() function
  47:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_wwdg.c ****               
  48:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_wwdg.c ****       (#) Set the WWDG counter value and start it using WWDG_Enable() function.
  49:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_wwdg.c ****           When the WWDG is enabled the counter value should be configured to 
  50:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_wwdg.c ****           a value greater than 0x40 to prevent generating an immediate reset.     
  51:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_wwdg.c ****               
  52:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_wwdg.c ****       (#) Optionally you can enable the Early wakeup interrupt which is 
  53:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_wwdg.c ****           generated when the counter reach 0x40.
  54:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_wwdg.c ****           Once enabled this interrupt cannot be disabled except by a system reset.
  55:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_wwdg.c ****                   
  56:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_wwdg.c ****       (#) Then the application program must refresh the WWDG counter at regular
  57:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_wwdg.c ****           intervals during normal operation to prevent an MCU reset, using
  58:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_wwdg.c ****           WWDG_SetCounter() function. This operation must occur only when
  59:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_wwdg.c ****           the counter value is lower than the refresh window value, 
  60:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_wwdg.c ****           programmed using WWDG_SetWindowValue().         
  61:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_wwdg.c ****   
  62:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_wwdg.c ****     @endverbatim
  63:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_wwdg.c ****   ******************************************************************************
  64:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_wwdg.c ****   * @attention
